#lang r7rs
;; r7rs-lang-plan R4 / D5: referential transparency.  `my-list`'s template
;; refers to `list` free; R7RS says that identifier means what it meant where
;; the macro was DEFINED, so shadowing `list` at the use site must not change
;; the expansion and this prints (1).  R4's renaming hygiene (D5a) renamed
;; only the identifiers a template BINDS and printed #(1); this fixture was
;; its named failing test (an expected.xfail marker).  R10 closed it: the
;; lowering tracks lexical scope, local binders get unique names, and a
;; template's free identifiers are resolved in the macro's definition scope.
(define-syntax my-list (syntax-rules () ((_ x) (list x))))
(display (let ((list vector)) (my-list 1)))
(newline)
